## PART VII: LONG-TERM PROFESSIONAL TRAJECTORY

### 7.1 Academic Career Path

A Ph.D. in HROE positions the graduate for faculty appointments in:
- Industrial and Systems Engineering
- Mechanical Engineering (Robotics and Control)
- Human Factors and Ergonomics
- Operations Research

The interdisciplinary nature of the degree makes the HROE Ph.D. exceptionally competitive for positions at research universities seeking to build programs at the intersection of AI, automation, and human-centered design.

### 7.2 Industry Career Path

Industry demand is structural and accelerating. Hiring demand across robotics, AI, and engineering roles has diversified beyond incumbents to start-ups, reflecting the breadth of deployment contexts now emerging beyond automotive and electronics into healthcare, construction, and logistics. [GlobeNewswire](https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2025/11/06/3182255/0/en/Industrial-Robots-Research-Report-2025-Humanoid-AI-Driven-and-Collaborative-Robotics-Set-New-Benchmark-for-Adaptive-Flexible-and-Smart-Manufacturing-Automation.html)

